><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Different support providers play different roles during athletedevelopment, i.e.o Mothers and fathers = financial and emotional support;o Mentors = Sport-specific informational and technical (or coach-ing related) support;o Siblings and peers = fellow participants for practice and play.&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Access to coaching emerged as a point of difference for elite ath-letes across all support providers, when compared to communitylevel athletes.•Elite cricketers rely on multiple components of a complex systemas a means of reaching greater sporting expertise.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="0" rect="637.179993,153.108017,821.179993,245.108017"
/></highlight
